okay, last time!
if you have traversed the stairs (excludes mimics) you can request a
teleport to a known location else the request is denied and no info is
given away since the request was invalid.  schemes that allow you to
teleport to stairwells without knowing where they are, give away info.
schemes that move the cursor to the next appropriate symbol and require
verification suffer from the same problem, IMO (am i missing something
very subtle?).  you should only be able to make the request if you have
prior knowledge of the existence of the structure.  if there are multiple
stairway types on this level (i.e. like the towers with both an up
stairwell and an up ladder) you go to the next appropriate structure
but only if you've traversed that structure (no info is given away),
no wait, you can't teleport on the towers but if you could ...
finally, i think this is your question, what if a mimic is over the
requested stairwell and imitating it?  the same as a teleport request
that would land you on top of a monster, "Sorry ..." (no info given
away).

btw, in private mail i recieved a note from Keni Lorber with an
excellent suggestion (altho slightly non-conformal): support cap's
and control modes while teleporting (this may have come up before).
cap's would move you 8 squares in the requested direction and
control modes (my idea) would move in the requested direction until
you reach _verified_ architecture (again that all-important kludgy
verified bit).  thus if a known fountain or stairwell, etc. is within
line of sight, you could reach it easily.  i suppose the control mode
could get extended to monsters without being idiosyncratic.

whatever the outcome, i'd like to thank Leonard, et al. for raising
a good issue and dealing with it intelligently...

